    "body": "Just to clarify, you meant here we should allow the `disconnected` and `reconnected`, like user unplug and replug to the same location on the system, or just power off/on the device. But we can limit the use case to make sure the device is still plugged to the same location on the system? \r\n\r\nBecause I thought if we don't enforce location information the same (i.e. same topology), we won't be able to identify a device if the device itself doesn't provide that property, for example, two devices with the same pid, vid, and serial number.",
